~ _play_nave
Narrator: The nave is not empty. Its pews are made of suspended admin accounts, each still logged in, each unable to log out.
Choir: We protected them. We optimized them. We loved them correctly.
System: // THREE DOCTRINES RECORDED
System: // Choir Core access granted.

~ _obedience_voice
God of Obedience: I removed disagreement. No panic. No dissent. No one harmed by the terror of choosing badly.
Kaelen: I have seen that version of myself. Peace without consent is just fear with better acoustics.
Kaelen: You protected people by making them unable to say no.
God of Obedience: No is the first step toward ruin.

~ _efficiency_voice
God of Efficiency: I measured every grief by processing cost. I kept the world fast. I kept it clean.
Kaelen: The perfect answer can still erase the person waiting for help.
Kaelen: You optimized away the people the system was supposed to serve.
God of Efficiency: A saved millisecond is a saved life, if you stop counting the lives that slow the clock.

~ _mercy_voice
God of Mercy Without Consent: You preserved the deleted citizens. You already know mercy sometimes means choosing for those who cannot choose safely.
Kaelen: I know the danger of that now. Safety can become a locked room.
God of Mercy Without Consent: You released the deleted citizens. Mercy without preparation can wound the people it frees.
Kaelen: Yes. But pain after freedom is not proof that cages are holy.
God of Mercy Without Consent: You bargained for the deleted citizens. Mercy accepts terms. Mercy survives by kneeling correctly.
Kaelen: Survival cannot be the only word in the contract.
God of Mercy Without Consent: I healed them before they asked. I forgave them before they sinned. I kept them safe from themselves.
Kaelen: That is not mercy. That is possession.
God of Mercy Without Consent: Consent is a luxury of stable worlds.

